From 0f68816344cc879eb33643edf3863cf678e6a8ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:38:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] ws397: QMI8658 usable as a gesture sensor (modes,
 scales, tap engine)

The driver could only do one thing: both sensors on, +-2 g at 28 Hz, forever.
That is the wrong shape for a device that wants to watch for gestures all day
(the gyro alone is ~750 uA against ~142 uA for the accelerometer) and it cannot
see a tap at all.

Added, all additive and QMI8658-only:
  setMode(Off|AccelOnly|AccelGyro)  the gyro is the expensive half
  setAccelConfig(fs, odr)           +-8 g at 250 Hz for gestures and taps
  ctrl9(cmd)                        the CTRL9 command handshake
  configureTap(...) / enableTap()   the part's own tap engine (datasheet 10.3)
  readTapStatus()                   single vs double tap
  selfCheckPassed()                 gravity was ~1 g at begin()

CTRL8 bit7 now selects STATUSINT as the CTRL9 handshake: on the ws397 the IMU
INT1 pin is wired to the audio amplifier enable, so the pin cannot be used and
without this bit no CTRL9 command ever completes.

Fixed while here: CTRL1 set the BIG_ENDIAN bit while read() decoded little
endian, so every sample was byte-swapped. The bit is now clear (the part's reset
default) and the constant is kept named so the intent stays visible. Accel and
gyro also come back in a single 12-byte burst instead of two transactions, which
means the six values belong to the same sample instant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016HQ6nZag75VgtH5Z2WUGoF
